    "body": "Another quick update. Instead of layer-norm, if I just do:\r\n```python\r\ndef ln_nb(x, gamma):\r\n    mean = x.mean(dim=1, keepdim=True)  # (B, C, L) -> (B, 1, L)\r\n    return x - mean\r\n```\r\n\r\nThen I get:\r\n```\r\nIteration 0\r\nOutput diffs. Mean: 0.0, Max: 0.0\r\nGrad diffs. Mean: 0.0, Max: 0.0\r\n\r\nIteration 1\r\nOutput diffs. Mean: 0.0, Max: 0.0\r\nGrad diffs. Mean: 0.0, Max: 0.0\r\n\r\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\nRuntimeError: Function torch::jit::(anonymous namespace)::DifferentiableGraphBackward returned an invalid gradient at index 0 - got [8, 1, 1024] but expected shape compatible with [8, 512, 1024]\r\n```",
